# Dependencies & package-manager caches
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-cache/

# The pnpm 11+ build-script policy file is **committed**. The original reason
# to keep it machine-local was that CI ran pnpm 10, which cannot parse
# `allowBuilds`; since `packageManager` pins pnpm@12.4.1 for every consumer,
# that concern is gone — and pnpm 12 fails a fresh `--frozen-lockfile` install
# outright on unreviewed build scripts (strictDepBuilds defaults to true), so
# CI needs this file to exist. Approvals here are package-level, not
# machine-level; review any new entry like a dependency change.

# `lib/` is deliberately **tracked**, not ignored. It is the published bundle:
# `main` / `types` / `exports` all point into it, and DSH STORE validates a
# *fixed Git commit* without running install, prepare or build. A commit that
# only carries `src/` is therefore an uninstallable package even though `npm
# publish` looks fine (npm rebuilds via `prepublishOnly` and ships `files`).
# Keep it in sync with `src/` in the same commit — preflight P8 fails on drift.
# Only the staging dir below is scratch.
dist/

# npm pack artifacts
*.tgz

# Harness-internal scratch: drafts, plan docs, config dumps, session metadata.
# Contains environment references and session IDs; keep out of public repos.
.sisyphus/

# Environment & secrets (never commit real values)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# Scratch dumps from local verification runs — `node -e "…" > file` redirects,
# probe output, column listings. Transient by definition, and they routinely
# capture machine paths and host-profile layouts.
.*.txt
_*.txt
.probe-*

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Obsidian workspace config (user-local, opens at the repo root)
.obsidian/

# Personal Obsidian knowledge base — private content, never pushed to the public repo
docs/vault/
scripts/check-vault.mjs
scripts/check-testcounts.mjs

# Marketplace submission checklist — internal doc, keep out of repo
MARKETPLACE.md

# WorkBuddy workspace memory (session logs, local notes) — keep local
.workbuddy/

# Session records & task/plan exports — any conversation/plan dumps must
# never reach the public repo (session IDs, paths, environment references)
*.jsonl

# Local diagnosis / migration notes — machine paths, profile layout, session
# references. Same policy as above: published docs live under docs/*.md with
# product-facing names; these stay local.
docs/dsh-*.md
docs/oss-prompt-optimizer-*.md
